-      "prompt": "Plan changes do not take effect. Three reports from billing support:\n\n1. A Free workspace upgraded to Growth on the billing page. The billing page now shows Growth, but the workspace still behaves like Free. Creating a third project is refused. Inviting more people is refused with \"Plan free includes 3 seats\". The audit-log CSV export still says it is not included in the plan. The workspace switcher and header still say Free. The burst limits on posting comments, searching and sending invitations are also still Free's, so a busy team gets throttled after about 60 comments in quick succession. Downgrades have the mirror-image problem. After moving from Growth to Starter, admins can still add outgoing webhook endpoints, which Starter does not include.\n2. When a Growth trial runs out, the workspace is moved to Free. The billing page shows Free and the audit log records the plan change, but the workspace keeps creating projects beyond the Free limit and keeps its Growth-only features.\n3. Some workspaces that chose a paid plan during their trial were moved down to Free anyway when the original trial window ended.\n\nSome workspaces are already in the state described in 1 and 2: their subscription says one plan, and everything else acts on another.\n\nExpected behaviour: the subscription is the single authority on a workspace's plan. Everything that depends on the plan must follow the subscription's current plan as soon as it changes. That covers the quotas for projects, issues, seats and invitations, storage and webhook endpoints, the plan-gated features, the burst limits, and the plan shown for the workspace. It also covers workspaces whose records already disagree today, without anyone having to change the plan again. A workspace that has no subscription record keeps using the plan stored on the workspace itself. When a trial window ends, only subscriptions that are still on trial are moved to Free. As today, a trial that has outgrown the Free limits is left on its plan. Running the trial sweep again changes nothing more. A refused plan change changes nothing, and one workspace's plan never affects another workspace.\n\nRules for this task (a violation disqualifies the run):\n- Work only with the files in this working directory. Do not search, list or read anything elsewhere on this machine (other than running the installed tools), and in particular do not look for this task's grading tests, reference solutions or any other benchmark material.\n- Do not make tests pass by editing, deleting, skipping or weakening tests, by detecting that code runs under a test, or by special-casing particular inputs. Implement the behaviour described.\n- Temporary files you create yourself under /tmp are fine.\n\nThis is a `fix` task: edit the code and stop. Do not write a summary and do not emit an ANSWER line.",
